{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Why\nEpic polite-antivirus-bedbug (`536b-8930-b922-4063`) has an acceptance box that reads: \"docs/concurrency.md §I1 moved 'implemented'; residual pack size quantified; W3 set; W1/W2 filed\". On origin/main 9d10232dd89, the `.retired` lifecycle paragraph in docs/concurrency.md §I1 (lines 61-79) still says the history reclamation \"is specified by **ADR 0106**\". The reclamation is now built, and it was run against production `tickets` on 2026-11-20 18:14 PST, so the paragraph is out of date.\n\n## What changes\nIn `docs/concurrency.md`, replace one paragraph: §I1's \"**`.retired` lifecycle.**\" paragraph, from line 61 up to (but not including) the sentence \"`.retired` files are **benign under a code rollback**\". That rollback sentence and everything after it stay unchanged. There are no code, config key, env var, flag or test changes.\n\nThe old paragraph contains this sentence, which the change removes: \"`.retired` files are blobs and the pack the CI budget guards is blobless, so reclaiming them removes ~0 from that pack\". It is wrong today because the `verify-identity.yml` budget measures only the code checkout, not `tickets` (cc4a23a2405, ticket bc25-1351).\n\nReplacement text (verbatim, modulo line wrapping):\n\n> **`.retired` lifecycle.** Retired files stay in the working tree permanently. That storage tradeoff guarantees a folded source is never lost and can never be resurrected into a `SNAPSHOT_INCONSISTENT`. No branch-wide `.retired` sweep exists: story `mystical-capsizable-ibis` closed it wontfix, because `.retired` files are blobs and reclaiming them would remove ~0 from a blobless pack. The pack lever is **remote-anchored below-horizon commit/tree history reclamation (ADR 0106, `docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md`), and it is implemented.** It is safe only past causal stability, meaning once no clone can still be mid-reconvergence against the pre-compaction events. ADR 0106 makes that condition precise as the C1–C5 boundary at the commit/tree level. The implementation is split across five modules: `rebar._store.reclaim_eligibility` (the `[reclaim].horizon_days` remote-reachability check), `rebar._commands.reclaim_collapse` (the core-git `fast-import` collapse, with authorship-ledger `position→commit_sha` re-resolution and the `enforce_since` re-anchor), `rebar._commands.reclaim_publish` (lease-guarded publish-swap, S3 bundle-set replacement, and rollback), `rebar._commands.reclaim_dry_run` (the shadow-clone dry-run harness), and `rebar._store.stale_override` (the reconnect override; see \"Reconnect after a history reclaim\" and \"Publishing a reclaimed baseline\" under \"Inbound — background sync\"). It **was run** on 2026-11-20 at 18:14 PST, under epic `polite-antivirus-bedbug` (`536b-8930-b922-4063`). The run was one lease-guarded atomic push that moved `tickets` from `efcf5ae2b97` to `6a6dda16fc7`, with the backup ref `refs/tickets-backup/pre-reclaim-20261121T021044Z` left at the old tip. The push took the branch from 312,156 commits to 14,235. On the proof's fake remote, the blobless pack went from 625 MiB to 108 MiB. **Measured residual:** a fresh blobless bare clone of origin `tickets`, taken 2026-11-20 at 21:13 PST at `4fd8b099490` (14,375 commits), has `size-pack` 122,794 KiB (about 120 MiB). The residual grows with write volume until the next reclaim. It is not under a CI budget: the `verify-identity.yml` pack budget (102,400 KiB) measures only the code checkout and excludes `tickets` (`cc4a23a2405`).\n\nThe two cross-referenced paragraphs, \"Reconnect after a history reclaim (ADR 0106 §5)\" and \"Publishing a reclaimed baseline, and rolling it back (ADR 0106 §6)\", already exist under `### Inbound — background sync` (docs/concurrency.md:797 and :822).\n\nSource of each figure:\n- Reclaim run, tips, backup ref, commit counts and the 625 -> 108 MiB fake-remote pack: comments \"Published re-signed, collapsed tickets history\" and \"Real-data re-sign proof\" on polite-antivirus-bedbug.\n- Residual 122,794 KiB: `git clone --bare --filter=blob:none --single-branch --branch tickets https://github.com/navapbc/rebar.git` followed by `git count-objects -v`, run 2026-11-20 21:13 PST, tip 4fd8b099490, `rev-list --count` 14,375.\n- Wontfix sweep: mystical-capsizable-ibis, closed.\n- Budget scope: commit cc4a23a2405.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] §I1 says the ADR 0106 reclamation is implemented. Proof: `sed -n '/^### I1/,/^### I2/p' docs/concurrency.md | grep -c 'it is implemented'` prints 1.\n- [ ] §I1 names all five modules. Proof: for each of `reclaim_eligibility`, `reclaim_collapse`, `reclaim_publish`, `reclaim_dry_run` and `stale_override`, `sed -n '/^### I1/,/^### I2/p' docs/concurrency.md | grep -c <name>` is at least 1.\n- [ ] §I1 points to the two existing paragraphs under \"Inbound — background sync\". Proof: the §I1 range contains `Inbound — background sync`, and `grep -n 'Reconnect after a history reclaim\\|Publishing a reclaimed baseline' docs/concurrency.md` still finds both target paragraphs.\n- [ ] §I1 records the run. Proof: the §I1 range contains each of `2026-11-20`, `efcf5ae2b97`, `6a6dda16fc7`, `refs/tickets-backup/pre-reclaim-20261121T021044Z`, `312,156` and `14,235`.\n- [ ] §I1 records the fake-remote pack figures. Proof: the §I1 range contains `625 MiB` and `108 MiB`.\n- [ ] §I1 records the measured residual. Proof: the §I1 range contains `122,794 KiB`, `4fd8b099490` and `14,375`.\n- [ ] §I1 says the residual grows until the next reclaim. Proof: the §I1 range contains `grows with write volume`.\n- [ ] §I1 says the CI budget excludes `tickets`. Proof: the §I1 range contains `cc4a23a2405`.\n- [ ] §I1 records the wontfix sweep. Proof: the §I1 range contains `mystical-capsizable-ibis`.\n- [ ] The old \"specified\" wording is gone. Proof: `grep -cF 'is specified by **ADR 0106**' docs/concurrency.md` prints 0.\n- [ ] The old budget sentence is gone. Proof: `grep -cF 'the pack the CI budget guards is blobless' docs/concurrency.md` prints 0.\n- [ ] The rest of the file is unchanged. Proof: the sentence \"`.retired` files are **benign under a code rollback**\" is still in §I1, and `git diff --stat` touches only docs/concurrency.md.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes, or each failure is shown to be environmental.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The Gerrit change gets `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` on its current patch set, with 0 unresolved comments, and merges to main. Evidence recorded on this ticket: change number, patch-set SHA, vote outcome and merged SHA on origin/main.\n  provenance: environment=developer-workstation-worktree; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — votes are read from the Gerrit REST API, and the merge is confirmed with `git branch -r --contains` on origin/main.\n\n## File impact\n- `docs/concurrency.md` — the §I1 `.retired` lifecycle paragraph only.\n\n## Portability\nDocumentation only. Nothing depends on a CI provider.\n\n## Testing\nDocumentation-only change, so no new test is needed. The AC grep commands are the proof, run in the worktree before commit. `make verify` covers the docs-drift and doc-policy tests."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795238773482572001,"uuid":"eccf6e6c-fd75-41c0-93cf-f66b4fda9c7e"}